  "summary": "The study compares eight distinct MXene electrodes explicitly identified by composition, architecture, thickness, or mass loading: a thin Ti3C2Tx film, three Ti3C2Tx hydrogels, four Ti3C2Tx macroporous films, and one macroporous Mo2CTx film. Ti3C2Tx was synthesized by LiF/HCl etching and delaminated; macroporous films used sacrificial PMMA microspheres, whereas Mo2CTx was HF-etched and TBAOH-intercalated. The headline high-rate electrode was MP-Ti3C2 (0.43 mg cm\u22122, 13 \u03bcm), reaching 310 F g\u22121 at 10 mV s\u22121 and retaining 210 F g\u22121 at 10 V s\u22121. Hydrogel electrodes supplied the best volumetric result, 1,500 F cm\u22123 at 2 mV s\u22121; BET area, porosity, tortuosity, and most electrode-specific flake dimensions were not reported."
}